Subject: [PATCH 45/45] soc/tegra: pmc: mark the early instance synced too

tegra_pmc_sync_state() sets core_domain_state_synced on the probed tegra_pmc,
but tegra_pmc_core_domain_state_synced() returns the flag of early_pmc, a
separate static instance that only gets the rate and base copied over. The
Tegra20/30 regulator couplers ask the latter, so they never see the core
domain synced and hold the CORE rail at the bootloader voltage: 1.3 V on the
Surface RT, and through max-spread the CPU at 1.0 V or more, while the core
domain asks for 1.0-1.1 V and the CPU OPPs for 0.8 V.
---
 drivers/soc/tegra/pmc.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/tegra/pmc.c b/drivers/soc/tegra/pmc.c
index f8792b795..18e348609 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/tegra/pmc.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/tegra/pmc.c
@@ -4869,6 +4869,12 @@ static void tegra_pmc_sync_state(struct device *dev)
 	 * mark the domain as synced in this case.
 	 */
 	pmc->core_domain_state_synced = true;
+	/*
+	 * tegra_pmc_core_domain_state_synced() reads the early instance, which
+	 * is not the probed one: without this the regulator coupler never sees
+	 * the domain synced and keeps the CORE at the bootloader's voltage.
+	 */
+	early_pmc->core_domain_state_synced = true;
 
 	/* this is a no-op if core regulator isn't used */
 	mutex_lock(&pmc->powergates_lock);
